   "source": [
    "# 6. Logistic (sigmoid) function"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "942aded2",
   "metadata": {
    "papermill": {
     "duration": 0.01944,
     "end_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:44.446604",
     "exception": false,
     "start_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:44.427164",
     "status": "completed"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    ">We have df_prep_scores, which contains the total score for each observation. Now, we need to convert these scores into probabilities using the logistic (sigmoid) function:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 36,
   "id": "194fdf10",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2025-09-04T10:44:44.487251Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2025-09-04T10:44:44.486911Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2025-09-04T10:44:44.523522Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2025-09-04T10:44:44.522590Z"
    },
    "papermill": {
     "duration": 0.059177,
     "end_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:44.525324",
     "exception": false,
     "start_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:44.466147",
     "status": "completed"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Convert score to probability\n",
    "y_score = 1 / (1 + np.exp(-(df_prep_scores - min_score) / (max_score - min_score)))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Flatten to a 1D array\n",
    "y_score = y_score.values.flatten()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8ae28726",
   "metadata": {
    "papermill": {
     "duration": 0.019643,
     "end_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:44.564850",
     "exception": false,
     "start_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:44.545207",
     "status": "completed"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    ">Now, let's calculate once again the ROC-AUC score to assess model performance and visualize the effectiveness of the scorecard."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 37,
   "id": "8158ffdd",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2025-09-04T10:44:44.606512Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2025-09-04T10:44:44.606143Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2025-09-04T10:44:45.952024Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2025-09-04T10:44:45.950980Z"
    },
    "papermill": {
     "duration": 1.368721,
     "end_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:45.953914",
     "exception": false,
     "start_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:44.585193",
     "status": "completed"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "ROC-AUC: 0.9939\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "\n",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 500x500 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.metrics import roc_auc_score\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import roc_curve\n",
    "\n",
    "# Compute ROC-AUC\n",
    "auc = roc_auc_score(y, y_score)\n",
    "print(f\"ROC-AUC: {auc:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Compute ROC curve\n",
    "fpr, tpr, thresholds = roc_curve(y, y_score)  # Make sure 'thresholds' is defined!\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot the ROC Curve\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(5, 5))\n",
    "plt.plot(fpr, tpr, label=f'ROC Curve (AUC = {auc:.4f})', color='blue')\n",
    "plt.plot([0, 1], [0, 1], linestyle='--', color='gray')  # Random model line\n",
    "plt.xlabel('False Positive Rate')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('True Positive Rate')\n",
    "plt.title('ROC Curve')\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "602d3713",
   "metadata": {
    "papermill": {
     "duration": 0.077744,
     "end_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.052645",
     "exception": false,
     "start_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:45.974901",
     "status": "completed"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    ">\n",
    ">0.9 - 1.0 → Excellent."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "32d31ace",
   "metadata": {
    "papermill": {
     "duration": 0.020597,
     "end_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.094031",
     "exception": false,
     "start_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.073434",
     "status": "completed"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "# 7. Youden's J statistic\n",
    ">The optimal cutoff balances the True Positive Rate (TPR) and False Positive Rate (FPR). A common method is Youden’s J statistic:\n",
    ">\n",
    ">\\[\n",
    "J = TPR - FPR\n",
    "\\]\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 38,
   "id": "11867399",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.136930Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.136530Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.142411Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.141068Z"
    },
    "papermill": {
     "duration": 0.029384,
     "end_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.144199",
     "exception": false,
     "start_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.114815",
     "status": "completed"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Optimal Cutoff Probability: 0.6514\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Compute Youden's J statistic\n",
    "j_scores = tpr - fpr\n",
    "optimal_idx = np.argmax(j_scores)\n",
    "optimal_threshold = thresholds[optimal_idx]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Optimal Cutoff Probability: {optimal_threshold:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "10865e6c",
   "metadata": {
    "papermill": {
     "duration": 0.020602,
     "end_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.185997",
     "exception": false,
     "start_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.165395",
     "status": "completed"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    ">Convert Probability Cutoff to Score Cutoff\n",
    "To determine the equivalent score cutoff, reverse the logistic function:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\[\n",
    "\\text{Score} = \\text{min\\_score} + (\\text{max\\_score} - \\text{min\\_score}) \\times \\log\\left(\\frac{p}{1-p}\\right)\n",
    "\\]\n",
    "$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 39,
   "id": "ae1e06e5",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.229259Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.228913Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.234299Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.232923Z"
    },
    "papermill": {
     "duration": 0.02905,
     "end_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.235948",
     "exception": false,
     "start_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.206898",
     "status": "completed"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Optimal Score Cutoff: 675\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Convert probability cutoff to score cutoff\n",
    "optimal_score_cutoff = min_score + (max_score - min_score) * np.log(optimal_threshold / (1 - optimal_threshold))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Optimal Score Cutoff: {optimal_score_cutoff:.0f}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7ae4ccd6",
   "metadata": {
    "papermill": {
     "duration": 0.020841,
     "end_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.278099",
     "exception": false,
     "start_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.257258",
     "status": "completed"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    ">Now, classify customers into \"Good\" or \"Bad\" risk segments using the optimal cutoff:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2b442dc0",
   "metadata": {
    "papermill": {
     "duration": 0.02065,
     "end_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.319902",
     "exception": false,
     "start_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.299252",
     "status": "completed"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "# 8. Risk Category🔴🟢"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 40,
   "id": "47c532ff",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.363435Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.363058Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.806638Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.805245Z"
    },
    "papermill": {
     "duration": 0.46728,
     "end_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.808631",
     "exception": false,
     "start_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.341351",
     "status": "completed"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "Risk_Category\n",
       "Good    1682399\n",
       "Bad      347553\n",
       "Name: count, dtype: int64"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 40,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Assign risk category based on cutoff\n",
    "df_prep_scores['Risk_Category'] = np.where(df_prep_scores >= optimal_score_cutoff, \"Good\", \"Bad\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# View distribution\n",
    "df_prep_scores['Risk_Category'].value_counts()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "71d63342",
   "metadata": {
    "papermill": {
     "duration": 0.020883,
     "end_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.850761",
     "exception": false,
     "start_time": "2025-09-04T10:44:46.829878",
     "status": "completed"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    ">\n",
    ">- Customers above the cutoff → \"Good\" Risk (Low probability of default).\n",
    ">- Customers below the cutoff → \"Bad\" Risk (High probability of default).\n"
   ]
  },
